    "lead_id": "city_volunteer_portal:177491",
    "text": "Who We Are: Philly Reading Coaches (PRC) is an afterschool early literacy program funded by the Office of Children and Families and implemented by Out-of-School time (OST) providers. This is a unique chance for volunteers to make a real impact in their community and build meaningful connections with young learners by making reading exciting and fun! PRC takes place at 13 schools around the city. Click here to browse PRC Opportunities! | What We Do: PRC’s model combines early reading support, access to books, and civic engagement to strengthen foundational literacy skills and encourage a love..."
